This is a fork. As required by section 4(b) of that licence, the changes
carried here are stated:

  2026-09-21  A four-component picture whose own JP2 header declares the
              enumerated colour space CMYK (EnumCS 12, ITU-T T.800 Table I.1)
              now decodes to an *image.CMYK rather than to an *image.RGBA
              built from its first three components. Reading those four planes
              as red, green and blue discarded the black plate; on the
              reference picture that was 255 levels from poppler on every
              pixel, and it is now at most 2 over 2 440 044 samples. The
              multi-component transform, where a codestream signals one, is
              undone across the first three planes exactly as before; the
              fourth is outside it and is kept. Decode and
              DecodeWithUpsampling take the same decision, so the two entry
              points cannot disagree about what a file is.

              Files: color.go (convertToCMYK, convertToCMYKFloat, sameShape),
              decoder.go (isCMYK, picture, pictureUpsampled, toCMYK),
              cmyk_test.go, go.mod (module path).

The entries below were added on 2026-10-18; until then this file named only
the first change, although all of them had been made. Each names the pull
request that carries its full reasoning and measurement.

Changes to what is decoded or encoded:

  2026-09-25  #2   The 9/7 synthesis no longer crashes on a tile or image whose
                   origin is odd. Files: dwt.go, dwt_test.go.
  2026-09-29  #19  9/7 coefficients are carried as float32, as OpenJPEG carries
                   them, in place of float64 in a second buffer. Files:
                   decoder.go, dwt.go, dwt_test.go, dwtpasses_test.go,
                   encoder_test.go, packet.go.
  2026-09-29  #23  The encoder anchors the code-block grid at the reference grid
                   (ITU-T T.800 B.7), where the decoder always anchored it.
                   Files: blockgrid.go, encoder.go, packet.go, tilegrid_test.go.
  2026-09-29  #24  The encoder is given each tile's position as well as its size;
                   a tiled encode had produced a codestream that this decoder
                   and OpenJPEG both read wrongly. Files: blockgrid.go, dwt.go,
                   dwt_encode.go, encoder.go, tilegrid_test.go.
  2026-09-29  #25  The forward 9/7 transform scales a resolution one row high,
                   as the inverse does. Files: dwt_encode.go, tilegrid_test.go.
  2026-09-29  #26  The decoder accepts a tile none of whose code blocks is
                   included in any packet, as the reference does. Files:
                   packet.go, allzerotile_test.go.

